Taken together, [[Ganan]], [[Taban]], and [[Venturan]] form the island's main population spine, with the capital corridor carrying the densest settlement and the strongest commuter links. [[Barian]] is the next growth belt, while the inland and highland districts thin out quickly. [[Bukan]] and [[Yukuman]] are the sparsest mainland districts. The district apportionment totals 284 Assembly members, with the largest block in [[Ganan]] and the smallest in [[Warikú]].

== Historical background ==

The district system is old. The 16 mainland districts preserve the territorial logic of the colonial era, even though their names were changed after the 1947 constitution to replace the old saint forms with pre-colonial Guaji names. [[Warikú]] was added as a separate seventeenth district after the war.

The result is a system that is administratively conservative but symbolically postcolonial: the boundaries are inherited, the names are local, and the population now clusters where trade, government, and transport are most tightly linked.

